sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Sender
    participant N as Nostr relays<br/>WebTorrent trackers
    participant R as Receiver

    Note over S: 32 random bytes from the CSPRNG
    S-->>R: QR code, carried by light and a camera
    Note over S,R: room ID, signalling password, session keys and the SAS all derive from those 32 bytes

    S->>N: announce, on every network at once
    R->>N: announce, on every network at once
    N-->>S: peer found
    N-->>R: peer found
    Note over S,R: session descriptions, AES-GCM under the derived password

    S-->>R: WebRTC data channel opens
    Note over S,R: ephemeral ECDH — one key per direction, per session
    Note over S,R: four emoji, read aloud, matched by hand

    S->>R: manifest (name, size) — only once the SAS is confirmed
    R->>S: accept — the same click that opens the save picker
    S->>R: file chunks, each one sealed by us
